            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0433" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/570: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-26T11:00:00-00:44">May 26, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. Referring to my 159, May 22. Von Waldheim, new German Consul, arrived and
                    five Germans left Monrovia by same French plane May 24. Those departing, Wehrle,
                    Kirstein, Fleck, Jantzen and Von Dein. Other Germans now planning to leave by
                    June 6th. Secretary Simpson states that for the moment Von Waldheim will be
                    allowed to remain here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
